.TH HD-NETWORK-BRIDGE 8 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-network-bridge \- add, change and remove bridges in the hyprdebian network settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-network-bridge list
.br
.B hd-network-bridge show
.I name
.br
.B hd-network-bridge set
.I name
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B hd-network-bridge remove
.I name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-network-bridge
manages the bridges in the key
.B hd-network
in
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json .
See
.BR hd-network (7)
for the settings.
.PP
It reads all the network settings, makes the change, checks the result the
same way
.BR hd-network-render (8)
does, and writes it with
.BR hd-config-update (1).
When the check fails, nothing is written.
When no settings are left, the key is removed with
.BR hd-config-remove (1).
.PP
Ports are added to a bridge with
.BR hd-network-iface (8):
.BI "hd-network-iface set " interface " \-\-bridge " name\fR.
.PP
It does not change the network itself: run
.B hd-network-render
afterwards.
.PP
.B set
and
.B remove
are run as root.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the bridges, one per line, with their MAC address, their ports and a
summary of their settings.
.TP
.BI show " name"
Show the settings of a bridge as JSON.
.TP
.BI set " name"
Add a bridge, or change its settings.
Settings that are not given stay as they are; a new bridge without options
uses DHCP.
A new bridge gets a random, locally administered MAC address, which is kept
in the settings, so it never changes, also not when the machine-id changes.
.TP
.BI remove " name"
Remove a bridge from the settings.
A bridge that still has ports is not removed; remove or change the ports
with
.B hd-network-iface
first.
.SH OPTIONS
These options are for
.BR set .
.TP
.BI \-\-mac " mac"
The MAC address of the bridge, such as
.BR 52:54:00:12:34:56 .
.TP
.B \-\-dhcp
Get addresses with DHCPv4, IPv6 router advertisements and DHCPv6.
This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-dhcp
Do not use DHCP or router advertisements.
.TP
.BI \-\-address " address/prefix"
A static address, such as
.BR 192.168.1.10/24 .
May be given more than once; replaces the addresses that were set.
.TP
.BI \-\-gateway " address"
The default gateway.
May be given more than once, for IPv4 and IPv6; replaces the gateways that
were set.
.TP
.BI \-\-dns " address"
A DNS server.
May be given more than once; replaces the DNS servers that were set.
.TP
.BI \-\-metric " n"
The metric of the routes; the default is 100.
.TP
.BI \-\-unset " setting"
Return a setting to its default before the other options are applied:
.BR addresses ,
.BR dhcp ,
.BR dns ,
.B gateway
or
.BR metric .
May be given more than once.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the command succeeded, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
A bridge for virtual machines with enp3s0 as its port, using DHCP:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-bridge set br0
hd-network-iface set enp3s0 \-\-bridge br0
hd-network-render
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove it again, with enp3s0 back on DHCP:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-iface set enp3s0 \-\-unset bridge
hd-network-bridge remove br0
hd-network-render
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-network (7),
.BR hd-network-iface (8),
.BR hd-network-render (8),
.BR hd-config-update (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
